      "evidence": [
        "README explicitly says the source artifact is preserved and labels the historical path as Source artifact.",
        "The cited summary path is absent relative to code/ and repository root; the tier-1 index is also absent.",
        "_latest_tier1_summary returns (None,None,[]) when index.json is absent. _fallback_body then renders fixed literals from _fallback_tier1_representative_rows with no missing-index warning.",
        "Both README render checks pass, so the unsupported provenance wording is in the generator as well as generated README.",
        "A bounded search found no matching artifact entry in the documentation evidence/archive; no assertion is made that the original file cannot exist outside this checkout."
      ],
      "impact": "A reader can mistake retained generator values for currently inspectable historical evidence; the no-requalification warning does not establish preservation or provenance.",
      "requested_fix": "Keep historical values and the no-requalification warning, but make fallback wording state that the values are retained in generator rows, the cited original artifact is unavailable in this checkout, and lineage/measurements were not verified. When a real artifact is loaded, describe only that observed state.",
